# Exercise: Combining Combinators
#
# The real power comes from combining dip, keep, and bi together.
#
# Pattern: compute multiple things from inputs without stack juggling.
#
# Example - format a labeled value:
#   "score" 42
#   [ int->string ] dip         — convert 42 to "42", preserve "score"
#   ": " string.concat swap string.concat  — build "score: 42"
#
# Your task: Given two numbers (a b), compute both their sum AND product
# using combinators instead of stack juggling.
# Stack starts: ( 3 7 )
# Result: ( 10 21 ) — sum on bottom, product on top
#
# Approach: use bi on the pair:
#   1. Use keep on the first value to preserve it
#   2. Then compute sum and product
#
# Hint: compute the product first with 2dup, then use dip to
# compute the sum underneath it.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

# Compute sum and product of two numbers using combinators
: sum-and-product ( Int Int -- Int Int )
    # Your code here
    # Given ( a b ) produce ( a+b a*b )
    # Try: 2dup i.* [ i.+ ] dip
    drop 0 0
;

: test-combine ( -- )
    3 7 sum-and-product

    # Do not edit below this line
    # Top should be 21 (product)
    21 test.assert-eq
    # Second should be 10 (sum)
    10 test.assert-eq
;
